            <div xml:id="d694">

                <pb facs="0829" n="821" xml:id="pg821"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.3382/30: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Walton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-08T18:00:00-04:00">September 8, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>39. If no objection is perceived, please inquire confidentially of Foreign Office
                    if visit of new 10,000 ton cruiser U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Boise</hi>
                    to Monrovia from October 24 to 27 would be agreeable, requesting that the usual
                    courtesies and facilities be accorded the vessel.</p>
                <p>Please telegraph reply, upon receipt of which additional details will be
                    furnished you.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
